#!/usr/bin/env bash
# PostToolUse hook (matcher: Edit|Write). Nudges the agent to also record
# memory-worthy content into findings-memory when it writes a Claude Code
# per-project auto-memory TOPIC file - skips MEMORY.md itself (just an index,
# not new content) and every other Write/Edit.
#
# PostToolUse can't block (the tool already ran by the time this fires) and
# does NOT support hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext (that's
# UserPromptSubmit's mechanism, not this event's - verified against
# code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md, not assumed). The only way this event can
# surface anything to the agent is: exit 2 -> stderr is shown to Claude as
# context on the already-completed call. Exit 0 -> stderr goes to the debug
# log only, invisible to the agent. So exit 2 here is not a failure signal,
# it's the delivery mechanism.
set -euo pipefail

file_path="$(python3 -c '
import json, sys
try:
    d = json.load(sys.stdin)
except Exception:
    print("")
else:
    print(d.get("tool_input", {}).get("file_path", ""))
')"

case "$file_path" in
  */memory/MEMORY.md) exit 0 ;;
  */memory/*.md)
    cat >&2 <<'NUDGE'
You just wrote a per-project auto-memory entry. This session also has a
cross-repo "findings" store - if it's worth surfacing outside this one repo,
also record it with `findings record`:
  - kind observation - a verifiable fact about how the CODE behaves (anchor
    with --file <path> --sha <sha>, or omit to auto-fill from HEAD).
  - kind memory --category process - how to work with the user (preferences,
    corrections, workflow habits) - not code-specific.
  - kind memory --category project - context specific to this repo (ongoing
    work, decisions, environment facts) that isn't itself a code claim.
Skip this if what you just wrote is genuinely local and not worth surfacing
elsewhere.
NUDGE
    exit 2
    ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;
esac
